-- Open the Omarchy menus with Latin input instead of Hangul.
--
-- A menu opened while the input method is in Hangul mode cannot be searched:
-- what you type goes through the composer and never matches an entry. The
-- wrapper switches the input method to Latin first, then runs the real command.
--
-- Installed to ~/.config/minsoft1115/hypr/ by setup-korean.sh, which adds one
-- require line to ~/.config/hypr/hyprland.lua between markers. Omarchy's own
-- bindings.lua is never edited.
--
-- The lines below are filled in by the script rather than written here, because
-- the command behind each key differs between Omarchy versions. The script reads
-- it out of Omarchy's own defaults and wraps whatever it finds, so an upgrade
-- that renames a command does not leave a binding pointing at nothing.
__BINDINGS__
